{
 "_about": {
  "source": "The Wrenfield events demo (wrenfield.example), published on the local stack, read 2026-11-16.",
  "served": "Records as its MCP server returns them (nxis_get): form inputs and report tokens trimmed. The index splits an event page into one record per type and drops offers and location from most, so these are thin.",
  "page": "The same events as their pages state them (the demo's data/events.json, venues.json, people.json) in schema.org, with the @ids the served corpus gives them. The ticket form is the served action in the shape the autofill runner records: nxis:targetKind selfPage and nxis:pageUrl beside nxis:observedUrl and nxis:bindingPending. validFrom is each pass's sale start. The demo has no cancelled, postponed or online-only event: tests derive those from these records by changing eventStatus or eventAttendanceMode."
 },
